I *finally,* after 5 years of playing, ascended a valkyrie named Brynhildr.

I got lucky and found a magic lamp in minetown, blessed it and got a 
wish (+2 blessed gray dragon scale mail) and then, later, found a very 
large hardware store with 2 more magic lamps. I managed to get Excalibur 
around level 8. All good, except I lost my pet in the gnomish mines.

Oddly, despite a lot of sacrificing, I never did get Mjollnir - I had to 
use a wish once I reached the castle for it. And having been burned by 
Rodney way too many times, I used a wish for Magicbane, too. I also 
wished for two scrolls of genocide to get rid of liches and mind flayers.

One of the biggest parts of my game was when I reached Orcus' lair - he 
managed to summon Yeenoghu, who summoned Demogorgon. I had only ever 
faced Demogorgon once, and he kicked my keister, so I was afraid it was 
all over. I knew I had to kill them off or they'd just keep following 
me. Luckily, I had a ring of conflict so when they summoned nasties it 
wasn't bad. I just keep applying with my unicorn horn, stood near the 
stairs, and threw Mjollnir at them repeatedly until they were gone. Once 
I had defeated them, I knew I had an ascendable character.

I got the amulet without too much of a hitch and got out as fast as 
possible. The amulet kept bouncing me backwards, but I made it out. 
After that, the biggest problem I had was finding the portal from the 
plane of fire to the plane of water. I didn't find the plane of air too 
bad because I had -29 AC and 339 HP.

Once I got to the astal plane I got lucky because my god's altar was the 
first one I came to and I only had to face Pestilence, some priests and 
some insects to get there. I sacrified the amulet and game over.

Mad props to Maniac for his Ascension Guide, which I found very useful. 
It feels good to finally have gone the distance!

